b-id-type="pmid">202996</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Andrews</surname><given-names>GD</given-names></name><name><surname>Lavin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Methylphenidate increases cortical excitability <italic><italic>via</italic></italic> activation of alpha-2 noradrenergic receptors</article-title><source>Neuropsychopharmacology</source><year>2006</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>594</fpage><lpage>601</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15999146</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anselmo-Franci</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Peres-Polon</surname><given-names>VL</given-names></name><name><surname>da Rocha-Barros</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Moreira</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Franci</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rocha</surname><given-names>MJA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>C-fos expression and electrolytic lesions studies reveal activation of the posterior region of locus coeruleus during hemorrhage induced hypotension</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>1998</year><volume>799</volume><fpage>278</fpage><lpage>284</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9675311</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Appel</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name><name><surname>Elde</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The intermediolateral cell column of the thoracic spinal cord is comprised of target-specific subnuclei: evidence from retrograde transport studies and immu